    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ēvectus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		in-evehi, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>borne</i> or <i>mounted upon</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne quisquam ... Iret inevectus caelum super,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. Cul. 339</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tendit inevectus radios Hyperionis ardor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 100</span></i>
			.</div>
